+# AutoVideoAI 7.0.71 — Flow duplicate-spend guard
+
+## What went wrong (7.0.70)
+
+The Flow job `20261020-112139-how-to-stop-overthinking-8715` (shot_026, take 1) was
+retried through automatic recovery and job restarts. Flow's chat showed the same
+generation request several times, and each one was charged. Code review of 7.0.70
+found these ways a Flow video prompt could be sent again:
+
+1. **Standard/legacy editor path had no request journal.** A submission there was
+   not recorded, so a later retry could not see that it had already been sent.
+2. **The factory's "no usable media" retry called the provider again** when the
+   provider returned an error dictionary instead of raising. Only the journal stopped
+   this, and the legacy path did not write one.
+3. **Nothing compared a new prompt with prompts already in the Flow chat.**
+4. **Approval clicks were not tied to a request the app had just sent.** With
+   "Always approve" selected, Flow approves each card, so a repeated prompt is paid
+   for at once.
+5. **Resume reconciled image replacement by default** (`--replace-unresolved-images`
+   defaulted to on), which can start a second credit-bearing image request.
+
+The exact number of repeated sends per shot is not confirmed by the logs in this
+release. The fixes below cover every path listed above.
+
+## What 7.0.71 changes
+
+* **Write-ahead submit ledger, per take** (`<take>.mp4.submit-ledger.jsonl`). An
+  `intent` line is fsynced before the Send action, and `submitted` after it. Any
+  `intent`, `submitted` or unreadable line blocks every later submission for that
+  take file, including after a restart. A saved `.flow-request.json` also blocks.
+* **Per-job ledger and cap** (`flow_submission_ledger.jsonl`). Default cap: 20 intents
+  per job. To raise it, run `python3 cli.py v3 resume <job_id> --flow-submission-cap N`.
+  The new value is written to `flow_submission_cap.json` and logged.
+* **Check mode.** `engine/flow_submit_guard.check_only()` is process-wide. While it
+  is active, no new video prompt is sent and no approval card is clicked.
+* **Single gate before any browser action.** Every video request is checked first.
+  A take that has a recorded or unknown submission is recovered by download only.
+* **Duplicate-prompt check.** If the exact instruction is already visible in the Flow
+  chat and this job has no ledger record of that prompt, nothing is sent. The saved
+  request must be inspected instead. Sibling takes of the same shot, which share a
+  prompt, are still allowed because the job ledger already accounts for them.
+  A different job that reuses the same project and prompt text is blocked; clear the
+  chat or use a different project to continue.
+* **Approval only for the request the app sent.** A card is clicked only while that
+  request is awaiting approval, and each click is logged in the take ledger.
+* **Factory retries** run only when the take has never started a submission.
+* **Image replacement is off during resume.** Any job with saved Flow requests has
+  its replacement permission cleared when `run_job` starts. `--replace-unresolved-images`
+  on resume is ignored with a notice. Resume recovery never sets replacement on.
+* **Recovering a saved request never reaches the send step.** The recovery branch
+  returns the file or raises; it has no path to a new prompt.
+
+## What it does not do
+
+* It does not restart, edit or re-download the saved shot_026 request. Recovery of
+  that take is a separate, explicit step, and it requires the local Flow session.
+* It cannot prove that Flow's own "Always approve" setting will not approve a card
+  that the app did not send. The guard prevents the app from sending the request in
+  the first place. Turning "Always approve" off is a separate user decision.
+* It has no live Flow test in this environment. Behaviour is covered by the fake-bridge
+  tests in `tests/test_v771_flow_submit_guard.py`.
+
+## Install
+
+From the 7.0.70 installation folder, after extracting the 7.0.71 zip beside it:
+
+    python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.71/tools/update_v770_to_v771.py .            # dry run
+    python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.71/tools/update_v770_to_v771.py . --apply
+
+Stop the dashboard before `--apply`. Only code and this document are replaced.
+Outputs, saved jobs, browser profiles and channel profiles are never touched.
